* __naku le broda cu brode__ -- what's the deal with na being terminated with ku?  ku, as far as I understand, is meant to terminate sumti, which apparently na isn't. --mi'e ((tsali))

''ku'' terminates floating tenses, such as ''puku''. ''naku'' is an extension of this.

''ku'' has four functions in Lojban:
#terminates a LA/LE description (but not LA+name)
#terminates a ''quantifier+selbri'' description (semantically equivalent to ''quantifier LO selbri'')
#terminates a free-floating sumti tcita or FA (the last is mostly useful in answers to ''fi'a'' questions)
#terminates a free-floating negation (this use is __not__ elidable)
